system "Lock shared by interchangeable workers"

# Four workers take turns in a critical section guarded by one lock. No rule
# treats one worker differently from another, so the workers are declared
# interchangeable and 'zin check' explores one state per arrangement up to
# renaming them: 9 states instead of 48.

types
  interchangeable worker is one of ann, ben, cid, dot
  phase is one of idle, waiting, critical

state
  at is a map from worker to phase
  holder is one of ann, ben, cid, dot, nobody

initially
  at of every worker is idle
  holder is nobody

never
  some a in worker satisfies some b in worker satisfies a is not b and at of a is critical and at of b is critical
always
  holder is nobody implies (every w in worker satisfies at of w is not critical)
sometimes
  every w in worker satisfies at of w is waiting
always possible holder is nobody

action want(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is idle
  at of w becomes waiting

action enter(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is waiting and holder is nobody
  at of w becomes critical
  holder becomes w

action leave(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is critical
  at of w becomes idle
  holder becomes nobody

scenario "One worker holds the lock, another waits"
  want(ann)
  want(ben)
  enter(ann)
  reject enter(ben)
  expect holder is ann and at of ben is waiting
